  abstract = {Accurate and real-time traffic flow prediction is essential in alleviating traffic congestion. However, it is challenging to build an accurate and fast prediction model due to the highly nonlinear and spatio-temporal volatility of large-scale traffic data. In this regard, this paper proposes a transfer grammar spatio-temporal synchronization graph transformer for traffic flow prediction. In this method, the Louvain algorithm and the time sliding window are used to divide the spatial graph structure of the entire traffic network into several local spatio-temporal graph subgraphs. Then, the subgraph data with the most nodes is selected and pre-trained by a grammar spatio-temporal synchronization graph transformer (GSTSGFormer). Finally, some parameters of GSTSGFormer are pre-trained by transfer to train other subgraph data, and the remaining trainable parameters of GSTSGFormer are fine-tuned, which ensures the prediction accuracy of other subgraphs and improves the training efficiency. The simulation results on real data sets validate that the prediction performance of the proposed method outperforms the existing contrast methods.},
