  abstract = {Aiming at the problem that the traffic flow prediction model does not consider the road contextual correlation and implicit spatial dependency, a spatio-temporal traffic flow prediction model based on adaptive graph convolution (Transformer-Graph Convolutional Recurrent Network, TGCRN) is proposed, which extracts spatio-temporal features by using an encoder-decoder structure. The encoder part designs a convolutional multi-head self-attention mechanism to extract spatio-temporal features from both local and global perspectives, and uses a traffic pattern memory to augment the nodeâs pattern information to assist future prediction. The decoder part injects an adaptive graph convolution module into the recurrent neural network to capture both temporal and spatial dependencies and outputs future traffic scenarios. The model extracts the hidden spatial dependencies from the unknown graph structure without any a priori knowledge guidance and is able to model complex and dynamic spatio-temporal relationships. Extensive experiments based on four real traffic datasets confirm the effectiveness of our approach.},
