  abstract = {Traffic flow prediction is an important part of intelligent transportation systems, and accurate prediction results help to alleviate traffic congestion and optimize the allocation of transportation resources. However, traffic flow data is highly nonlinear and complex, and traditional prediction methods are difficult to capture its spatio-temporal dependence. To solve the above problems, this paper proposes a wavelet transform-based spatio-temporal feature fusion graph neural network (WSTFGNN) model. The model first uses wavelet transform to decompose the original traffic flow data into high and low frequency subsequences at different scales, in order to capture the changing features of traffic flow on time scale and space scale. Next, a spatio-temporal feature fusion mechanism is designed to effectively fuse the temporal and spatial features extracted by the wavelet transform to capture the spatio-temporal dependence of traffic flow more comprehensively. Finally, the fused features are utilized for traffic flow prediction. The experimental results show that compared with the existing baseline model, the WSTFGNN model achieves better prediction accuracy on several real traffic flow datasets, and especially exhibits stronger robustness when dealing with complex traffic conditions and unexpected events. The model provides a new idea for traffic flow prediction, which has important theoretical significance and practical application value.},
  publisher = {IEEE},
