  abstract = {Prediction of traffic congestion is one of the most important elements of intelligent transportation systems (ITS), particularly in rapidly urbanizing areas. This paper presents a real-time deep learning architecture that combines the strengths of Graph Convolutional Networks (GCNs) and Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks to learn both spatial relationships within traffic flows and temporal patterns of traffic behavior. The model trains on practical sensor data and predicts future traffic conditions based on the same inputs with high accuracy. The framework enables the discovery of underlying traffic patterns through effective modeling. It supports smarter decision-making in urban mobility planning and enables proactive traffic management. Experimental evaluations show the efficiency of the model across various performance metrics, making it highly suitable for deployment in modern smart city ecosystems. Moreover, the architecture remains scalable and operates in real time, providing consistent, secure, and timely information. Its modular design allows easy adaptation to different urban infrastructures and sensor networks.},
