  abstract = {This study proposes an innovative method for high-precision traffic flow prediction through the Fusion of Multi-source heterogeneous External dataâFME-GCN. By fusing various external factors, including weather conditions, temperature variations, POI, holidays, and traffic peak and valley periods, FME-GCN significantly enhances the modelâs perception capabilities. Additionally, by using a lookup function, FME-GCN increases the reference weight of traffic flow data with stronger correlations and improves the modelâs graph attributes by fusing the node adjacency matrix with POI attributes. Our experiments on the SZ-taxi, PEMS04 and PEMS08 datasets demonstrate that FME-GCN achieves a 1% to 8.1% improvement in prediction accuracy while maintaining a minimal increase in computational complexity (less than 1%). Furthermore, ablation studies further validate the significant contribution of the integrated external factors to the modelâs performance.},
