  year = {2025},
  pages = {8580--8585},
  doi = {10.23919/CCC64809.2025.11179276},
  url = {https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/stamp/stamp.jsp?arnumber=11179276},
  abstract = {The Automatic Identification System (AIS) has a wide range of applications in navigation safety and maritime management. However, due to the long broadcasting time interval of AIS, the real-time information update of ships is slow, and the ship trajectory is not smooth, which is not conducive to virtual traffic flow scene testing. To explore the patterns and trajectories of ship motion, this paper proposes a ship trajectory prediction method that can be used for traffic flow scene generation. Firstly, density based spatial clustering and noise point detection algorithms are used to cluster the historical trajectories of ships in the region, obtaining typical trajectories of ships in the area. Then, spatiotemporal graph convolutional neural network(STGCN) models are used to train the typical trajectories of the clustered ships separately, thus obtaining a fitted trajectory model of the ships. The STGCN model is used to enhance the continuity of the predicted trajectory by changing the time interval. Finally, compared with the forecast results of the two interpolation methods, the results showed that the interpolation effect based on STGCN was closer to the true value of the ship's navigation trajectory.},
