  abstract = {To address the challenges in pattern mining and understanding of traffic flow data with high dimensionality, non-linearity, and strong spatio-temporal correlations, this paper proposes an integrated framework named "Deep Spatio-Temporal Feature Learning - Clustering - Visualization" (DST-FCV). This framework combines deep learning with advanced visualization technologies. It extracts low-dimensional feature representations containing essential information from raw traffic flow data through Spatio-Temporal Graph Convolutional Networks (STGCN) and Spatio-Temporal Autoencoders (ST-AE). By introducing the idea of Deep Embedded Clustering (DEC), it performs end-to-end joint optimization of feature learning and clustering objectives, improving the accuracy and robustness of clustering. Moreover, it uses Uniform Manifold Approximation and Projection (UMAP) to map high-dimensional features or clustering results to 2D/3D space, and generates intuitive visual views by combining with geographic information. Experiments on datasets such as PeMS, HighD, and urban regional road network show that this framework significantly outperforms traditional methods and single deep learning methods in clustering metrics like Silhouette Coefficient (SC) and Adjusted Rand Index (ARI), as well as in visualization quality evaluation. It can effectively identify traffic states and patterns, providing decision support for intelligent transportation.},
