  abstract = {This paper proposes a reinforcement learning-driven dynamic attack path prediction and adaptive strategy optimization (DAPPA-ASO) algorithm to achieve highprecision attack path reasoning and active defense decision-making. Based on the spatiotemporal graph convolutional network (ST-GCN), this paper builds an attack behavior feature extractor to capture network topology and traffic timing characteristics. Secondly, a dual-duel deep $Q$ network architecture is designed. The main network iteratively optimizes the attack path prediction $Q$ value function through the Bellman equation, and the auxiliary network generates defense strategies based on the state-action reward function. The meta-strategy gradient mechanism is introduced to dynamically adjust the exploration-exploitation ratio using the meta-knowledge of historical attack scenarios to achieve rapid adaptation of defense strategies under variant attacks. On the CIC-IDS2017 dataset, the average accuracy of DAPPA-ASO is improved to 93.8%, successfully blocking an average of 91.5% of multi-step penetration attacks. Through the collaborative prediction-defense framework driven by reinforcement learning, this algorithm significantly improves the active defense capability in a dynamic network environment.},
