  abstract = {Spatiotemporal data associated with trajectories often contains missing parts due to device failures, data transmission errors, or intentional concealment. Developing eï¬cient methods to reconstruct the missing segments becomes highly critical. In this study, we propose the spatiotemporal complementary GNN (STCompGNN) model, which aims to address the problem of completing trajectories with large missing regions (i.e., complementary trajectories). While the spatial characteristic learning unit of STCompGNN, equipped with a graph attention network (GAT), learns the spatial features of the data, the temporal characteristic learning unit, which integrates attention mechanisms and GRU models, learns the temporal trends embedded in trajectory data. By jointly addressing both spatial and temporal aspects of spatiotemporal data, our model achieves high performance in trajectory completion and surpasses shortest path interpolation which is one of the few alternatives in the literature.},
