  url = {https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/stamp/stamp.jsp?arnumber=11227366},
  abstract = {The ER-TTE (En Route Travel Time Estimation) task provides driving information that the driver has already traversed during the current state, which allows us to extract the driverâs personalized information and thereby improve the prediction of the remaining route travel time. Existing ER-TTE tasks almost universally employ meta-learning methods, but they are sensitive to learning rate tuning and cannot sufficiently learn the personalized information of the drivers. To address these issues,We propose a simple and efficient model, DSER-TTE. Firstly, we extract driving preference and driving cycle features from the traveled trajectory. Secondly, we employ an attention mechanism to learn the relationship between driving preference and driving cycle, and generate driving style features. Lastly, we fuse these generated features with the spatio-temporal features learnt by mainstream TTE models and estimate the travel time.Extensive experiments on large-scale real-world datasets have demonstrated the effectiveness of the proposed DSER-TTE model.},
