  abstract = {Accurate and safe trajectory prediction is critical for intelligent connected vehicles in complex urban traffic. To address the limitations of existing methods in topological interaction modeling, scene-adaptive conservatism, and multimodal diversity, we propose DGAC-Net (Dual Graph Attention with Conservatism Constraint Network). Built on a spatiotemporal graph neural network, DGAC-Net enhances dynamic interaction modeling through topology-enhanced attention, introduces sceneaware conservatism constraints to improve trajectory rationality, and adopts an improved multimodal decoding objective to mitigate mode collapse. Experimental results show that DGACNet outperforms existing baselines in prediction accuracy while generating more conservative and realistic trajectories in complex scenarios.},
