  abstract = {Massive MIMO is pivotal to 5G and beyond, yet its benefits depend on accurate and timely Channel State Information (CSI) prediction under rapidly time-varying and nonlinear channels. We propose a Spectral Temporal Graph Transformer (STGT) that unifies graph-based spatial learning with transformer-based temporal attention to predict compressed CSI. The model dynamically constructs data-driven graphs, performs spectral filtering to capture multi-scale spatial dependencies, and leverages self-attention to learn long-range temporal evolution. Evaluations on realistic 3GPP TR 38.901 channel models across diverse SNR and mobility regimes show that STGT outperforms RNN/LSTM, vanilla transformers, and STEM-GNN in NMSE and spectral efficiency, while maintaining robustness under high mobility and aggressive compression. These findings indicate that STGT is a scalable, end-to-end framework for intelligent CSI prediction in next-generation wireless systems.},
