  url = {https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/stamp/stamp.jsp?arnumber=11622812},
  abstract = {Targeting the complex traffic states and insufficient systematic monitoring/control in expressway reconstruction and expansion work zones, this study develops a coordinated "prediction-control" framework with an integrated traffic operation monitoring and management platform, validated through Wuhu-Xuancheng Expressway project. The hierarchical architecture establishes a "data-perception-decision-application" technical chain. The infrastructure layer integrates multi-source data (navigation, toll, construction) to provide dynamic spatiotemporal data support. The middleware layer employs Dynamic Bayesian Graph Convolutional Network (DBGCN) for congestion identification, risk node detection, and multi-step traffic prediction, combined with Reinforcement Learning (RL) to generate safety-efficiency balanced optimal speed control strategies. The application layer enables interdepartmental coordination for efficient control implementation. This full-scenario platform addresses real-time monitoring, risk anticipation, and collaborative management, providing systematic yet practical solutions for work zone safety management. The technical framework offers reference value for similar engineering projects.},
