  abstract = {social media offers a wealth of real-time traffic data. However, transforming a high volume of noisy, ambiguous and unstructured posts into machine-readable knowledge is still a challenging task. In this paper, we present DTKG (dynamic traffic knowledge graph) that aims to automate structured extraction of traffic events from X (Formally twitter) by a combination of fine-tuned GPT-4o with schema-guided prompts, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), and Chain-of-Verification (CoVe), and finally a spatio-temporal extension of GraphSAGE is used for link prediction on the KG. 140k traffic-related tweets are used as the dataset. DTKG gains an extraction of the precision as $96 \%$, while recall and $F 1$ respectively $91 \%$ and $93 \%$. Moreover, reduces hallucinations from $\mathbf\{8 . 2\} \boldsymbol\{\%\}$ to $\mathbf\{2 . 1 \%\}$ via RAG-CoVe. Regarding graph completion, ST-GraphSAGE reaches MRR of $67 \%$ and Hits@ $\mathbf\{1 0\} \boldsymbol\{=\} \mathbf\{8 8 \%\}$, outperforming GraphSAGE and GAT some temporal GNNs. Nevertheless, Our analysis shows that combining RAGâs evidence retrieval with CoVeâs verification yields the largest improvement in the final knowledge graphâs quality. DTKG offers an accurate, scalable approach for ITS decision support.},
